1
00:00:02,859 --> 00:00:07,510
Lesson 21, Susan gets a surprise call.

2
00:00:08,859 --> 00:00:12,210
Donna, from the National Cookie Company, calls Susan.

3
00:00:12,759 --> 00:00:16,129
She wants to buy out Susan's scrumptious cookies.

4
00:00:16,899 --> 00:00:19,029
Susan is very happy.

5
00:00:20,359 --> 00:00:23,209
Hello, good afternoon.

6
00:00:23,699 --> 00:00:26,669
Are you Susan of Susan's scrumptious cookies?

7
00:00:27,179 --> 00:00:28,209
Yes I am.

8
00:00:28,579 --> 00:00:33,609
My name is Donna Jenkins, and I'm calling from the National Cookie Company.

9
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:38,629
We're nuts about your cookies, and we'd like to sell them all over the country.

10
00:00:39,879 --> 00:00:43,750
Unfortunately, we're running on a shoestring out of our kitchen.

11
00:00:44,179 --> 00:00:46,449
We can't make enough cookies for you.

12
00:00:46,899 --> 00:00:51,109
My company wants to buy the recipe and the brand name from you.

13
00:00:51,539 --> 00:00:52,250
Oh yeah?

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:54,309
Why would you want to do that?

15
00:00:54,660 --> 00:00:58,609
We have a successful track record of buying small companies,

16
00:00:59,039 --> 00:01:00,909
and turning them into big ones.

17
00:01:02,159 --> 00:01:05,770
In that case, I'm sure we can come to an agreement.

18
00:01:06,180 --> 00:01:09,030
Great. You just made my day.

19
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:13,670
You'll need to work out the nuts and bolts of the agreement with my husband.

20
00:01:14,219 --> 00:01:15,670
He's the business manager.

21
00:01:16,159 --> 00:01:17,469
May I speak with him now?

22
00:01:18,219 --> 00:01:19,210
He's at a meeting.

23
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:22,210
I'll have him get in touch with you when he returns.

24
00:01:22,060 --> 00:01:25,510
Good. I look forward to speaking with him.

